<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Campus Guidelines — Mensa</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,500..700&family=Instrument+Sans:wght@400..700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css" integrity="sha512-DTOQO9RWCH3ppGqcWaEA1BIZOC6xxalwEsw9c2QQeAIftl+Vegovlnee1c9QX4TctnWMn13TZye+giMm8e2LwA==" crossorigin="anonymous" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>
<body class="policy-body">
    <header class="app-header">
        <div class="landing-nav">
            <a href="/Mensa.app" class="nav-brand">
                <span class="nav-brand-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-burger"></i></span>
                <span class="nav-title">Mensa<span class="brand-dot"></span></span>
            </a>
            <div class="nav-actions">
                <a href="/Mensa.app" class="btn-secondary btn-sm nav-auth-btn">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i>
                    <span>Back to home</span>
                </a>
                <% if (typeof currUser !== 'undefined' && currUser) { %>
                    <a href="/Mensa.app/logout" class="btn-secondary btn-sm nav-auth-btn">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right-from-bracket"></i>
                        <span>Log out</span>
                    </a>
                <% } %>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>

    <%-include("./includes/flash.ejs")%>

    <main class="policy-main">
        <div class="policy-container">
            <div class="policy-header">
                <div class="policy-badge"><i class="fa-solid fa-compass"></i> Student & Staff Charter</div>
                <h1 class="policy-title">Campus Guidelines</h1>
                <p class="policy-subtitle">Community standards and etiquette for hassle-free canteen ordering, timely pickups, and counter safety.</p>
                <div class="policy-meta">
                    <span><i class="fa-regular fa-clock"></i> Last updated: October 2026</span>
                    <span><i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i> Mensa Campus Operations</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Policy Navigation Tabs -->
            <nav class="policy-nav-tabs">
                <a href="/Mensa.app/guidelines" class="policy-tab active"><i class="fa-solid fa-book-open"></i> Guidelines</a>
                <a href="/Mensa.app/terms" class="policy-tab"><i class="fa-solid fa-scale-balanced"></i> Terms of Service</a>
                <a href="/Mensa.app/privacy" class="policy-tab"><i class="fa-solid fa-user-shield"></i> Privacy Policy</a>
            </nav>

            <div class="policy-card">
                <section class="policy-section">
                    <div class="section-icon-header">
                        <span class="icon-circle"><i class="fa-solid fa-ticket"></i></span>
                        <h2>1. Counter Pickup & Token Protocol</h2>
                    </div>
                    <p>Mensa is designed to eliminate chaotic counter crowds and long standing queues between academic periods. To ensure a smooth experience for everyone:</p>
                    <ul class="policy-list">
                        <li><strong>Live Token Verification:</strong> Always present your live order status screen with your designated Order Number at the canteen pickup counter. Screenshots from other devices or altered tokens are strictly invalid.</li>
                        <li><strong>Wait for the "Ready" Alert:</strong> Do not crowd the preparation counter before your order status changes to <span class="badge-inline green">Ready</span>. Gathering in front of serving bays obstructs staff and slows down cooking.</li>
                        <li><strong>15-Minute Pickup Grace Period:</strong> Once marked Ready, food must be collected within 15 minutes to guarantee peak freshness and food hygiene standards. Unclaimed food may be discarded after the grace period without refund.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <section class="policy-section">
                    <div class="section-icon-header">
                        <span class="icon-circle"><i class="fa-regular fa-calendar-check"></i></span>
                        <h2>2. Time-Slot Scheduling & Pre-Orders</h2>
                    </div>
                    <p>Pre-ordering allows canteen kitchens to prep high-demand meals before rush hours:</p>
                    <ul class="policy-list">
                        <li><strong>Arrival Windows:</strong> When selecting a specific time slot (e.g. 1:00 PM – 1:30 PM), arrive within your reserved half-hour window. Kitchen capacity is calculated dynamically based on reservations.</li>
                        <li><strong>Cancellation Window:</strong> Slot reservations can only be canceled while status is <span class="badge-inline amber">Pending</span>. Once the kitchen begins meal prep (<span class="badge-inline">Preparing</span>), slot cancellations are locked.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <section class="policy-section">
                    <div class="section-icon-header">
                        <span class="icon-circle"><i class="fa-solid fa-utensils"></i></span>
                        <h2>3. Canteen Hygiene & Waste Segregation</h2>
                    </div>
                    <p>Mensa actively champions clean and sustainable university campuses:</p>
                    <ul class="policy-list">
                        <li><strong>Tray Return:</strong> After finishing your meal, return reusable plates and trays to the designated scullery / wash station.</li>
                        <li><strong>Waste Disposal:</strong> Segregate organic food scraps and recyclables (paper wraps, cans) into their respective disposal bins.</li>
                        <li><strong>Outside Food:</strong> Consumption of outside commercial food within canteen seating areas is subject to the individual university canteen's campus regulations.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <section class="policy-section">
                    <div class="section-icon-header">
                        <span class="icon-circle"><i class="fa-solid fa-handshake-angle"></i></span>
                        <h2>4. Mutual Respect & Zero Tolerance for Harassment</h2>
                    </div>
                    <p>Canteen personnel, cooking staff, and student volunteers are an indispensable part of campus life:</p>
                    <ul class="policy-list">
                        <li>Verbal abuse, aggressive behavior, pushing in queues, or mistreatment of kitchen staff will lead to immediate suspension of your Mensa account and referral to the University Proctorial Board.</li>
                        <li>If you experience an order issue, incorrect item, or billing discrepancy, politely notify the counter manager or file a report through our <a href="mailto:kumar47nikhil@gmail.com">support desk</a>.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <section class="policy-section">
                    <div class="section-icon-header">
                        <span class="icon-circle"><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i></span>
                        <h2>5. Dietary Disclaimers & Allergies</h2>
                    </div>
                    <p>While canteen menus mark items with vegetarian and food indicators, university kitchens operate shared prep counters. Students with severe allergies (nuts, gluten, dairy) must verify ingredients directly with the head chef prior to consuming pre-ordered meals.</p>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>

    <%-include("./includes/footer.ejs")%>
    <script src="/script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
